## AssistantPlugin

Internal `IAssistantPlugin` implementation that configures the API References extension for each kernel/chat instance.

### Namespace
`Cyrena.APIReferences.Services`

### Access Modifier
`internal`

### Implementation

```csharp
internal class AssistantPlugin : IAssistantPlugin
{
    public string[] Modes => [DevelopOptions.AssistantModeId];
    public int Priority => 20;
    public string Id => "cyrena.api_references";
    public bool Required => true;
    public string Title => "API References";

    public Task LoadAsync(CyrenaKernelBuilder builder)
    {
        var persistence = builder.GetFeatureOption<ICyrenaPersistenceBuilder>();    
        persistence.AddSingletonStore<ApiReference>("api_references");
        builder.Plugins.AddFromType<APIReferences>();
        builder.AddToolbarComponent<ToolbarIcon>(ToolbarAlignment.End);
        return Task.CompletedTask;
    }
}
```

### Plugin Properties

| Property | Value | Description |
|----------|-------|-------------|
| `Id` | `"cyrena.api_references"` | Unique plugin identifier |
| `Title` | `"API References"` | Human-readable name |
| `Modes` | `[DevelopOptions.AssistantModeId]` | Only loads in developer assistant mode |
| `Priority` | `20` | Load order priority |
| `Required` | `true` | Cannot be deactivated |

### LoadAsync Behavior

1. **Register Store:** Gets `ICyrenaPersistenceBuilder` from feature options and registers `IStore<ApiReference>` as a singleton with collection name `"api_references"`.
2. **Register Kernel Plugin:** Adds `APIReferences` as a Semantic Kernel plugin via `builder.Plugins.AddFromType<APIReferences>()`.
3. **Register Toolbar Component:** Adds `ToolbarIcon` component to the chat toolbar at `ToolbarAlignment.End`.

### Dependencies
- `ICyrenaPersistenceBuilder` from `Cyrena.Persistence.Core` (via feature options)
- `DevelopOptions` from `Cyrena.Coding.Core` (for mode filtering)
- `ToolbarIcon` component (referenced but **currently missing** from `Components/Shared`)

### Mode Restriction
This plugin only loads when the chat's assistant mode matches `DevelopOptions.AssistantModeId`. This means API References functionality is only available in developer/coding assistant mode.
